icaâ€™s last colony: â€ Covering an area the size of Britain, Western Sahara is designated as a â€œnon-self-governing territoryâ€ by the United Nations and remains on its official list of territories still awaiting decolonization. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:9] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: Retained by Francisco Francoâ€™s Spain even as other European colonies won their freedom, it did not gain independence even after the dictatorâ€™s demise in 1975. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:10] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: Instead, neighboring Morocco and Mauritania invaded â€” with at least 40 percent of the Sahrawi population at the time fleeing to neighboring Algeria to escape the Moroccan air forceâ€™s bombing campaign. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:11] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: Half a century later, 173,000 Sahrawis still remain in Algerian refugee camps. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:12] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: The native Sahrawis living under Moroccan occupation are subject to what Freedom House categorizes as among the least free political systems on the planet. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:13] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: The Odyssey is the first major Hollywood production to shoot scenes in Western Sahara. (attribute: https://africasacountry.com/2026/07/odyssey-to-africas-last-colony)\n  - [claim:odyssey-to-africa-s-last-colony:14] Odyssey to Africaâ€™s last colony: This would have been unthinkable prior to 2020, when President Donald Trump broke with decades of US